WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.063
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.063 --> 00:00:01.896
- Well-

00:00:01.896 --> 00:00:05.179
- Man, y'all both have like
the rock and roll jackets

00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:06.807
going on right now.

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:08.023
I like the rock and roll jackets.

00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:08.856
Have you ever met Jeff?

00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:09.689
Have you ever met?

00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:10.522
- No, I haven't.

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:11.355
- This is the first time we've ever met.

00:00:11.355 --> 00:00:12.188
So nice to see you.

00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:13.021
- Yeah.

00:00:13.021 --> 00:00:14.139
- I like to bring people together.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:14.972
- You're doing it.

00:00:14.972 --> 00:00:15.805
You're doing the thing.

00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:16.638
- I have to ask you really,

00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:17.497
a professional hockey player.

00:00:17.497 --> 00:00:18.330
When did this start?

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.163
- I did.

00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:19.996
- It just seems an odd thing-

00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:22.394
- Very odd for being in the southeast.

00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:23.227
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:23.227 --> 00:00:25.420
- Yeah, not the traditional
sports down there.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.381
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:26.381 --> 00:00:27.838
- My dad, my stepdad was a hockey player.

00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:28.746
He grew up in Minnesota.

00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:29.579
- [Kelly] Oh, that's cool.

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:31.655
- So he sort of just threw me on the ice

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:33.401
at like seven years old and was like-

00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:34.234
- That's smart.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.067
- Figure it out.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:35.900
- Yeah.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.167
- And I fell in love with
falling on my face a lot.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.404
(laughing)

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.741
And eight concussions later
and a torn rotator cuff,

00:00:40.741 --> 00:00:43.265
I was like this is probably
not the career path for me.

00:00:43.265 --> 00:00:44.509
- I think you're supposed
to stop after three-

00:00:44.509 --> 00:00:46.179
Concussions.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.849
- That would've been really
good to know at the time,

00:00:47.849 --> 00:00:49.330
but I just kept going.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.360
- So did you ever wanna be
anything other than actor?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.193
- No.

00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:54.175
No.

00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:56.467
No, but my family,

00:00:56.467 --> 00:01:00.694
we had a shuffle board
court in our backyard,

00:01:00.694 --> 00:01:02.156
so I played a little shuffleboard

00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:04.788
and then I was in Stevanker
and I did some curling.

00:01:04.788 --> 00:01:05.621
That's all I'll tell you.

00:01:05.621 --> 00:01:07.253
- Were you the one-on-one
knee or were you-

00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:08.766
- Yes and the brooming.

00:01:08.766 --> 00:01:09.599
I did both.

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:10.628
I did the brooming and I did the thing.

00:01:10.628 --> 00:01:11.461
- Okay.

00:01:11.461 --> 00:01:13.260
- It's the funniest sport to
me just to see someone going-

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.093
- Well-

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.443
- I was in Italy a couple months back

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.552
and I was stuck in the hotel waiting for,

00:01:18.552 --> 00:01:19.580
it was a delayed flight

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.956
and there was curling on

00:01:20.956 --> 00:01:21.966
and it was in Italian

00:01:21.966 --> 00:01:22.991
and I was so fascinated.

00:01:22.991 --> 00:01:23.824
I was like-

00:01:23.824 --> 00:01:24.657
- How random.

00:01:24.657 --> 00:01:25.708
- Why is this happening in
Venice, Italy right now?

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:26.541
(laughing)

00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:27.709
- [Kelly] Like why am I still watching it.

00:01:27.709 --> 00:01:29.197
- I loved it, I loved it.

00:01:29.197 --> 00:01:30.030
- [Kelly] Yeah, you're
like in love with it.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:30.863
- I was into it.

00:01:30.863 --> 00:01:31.696
- Okay so Chase,

00:01:31.696 --> 00:01:32.529
do you remember the first time you thought

00:01:32.529 --> 00:01:33.808
about being an actor since
you were so into hockey?

00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:35.092
Like when did you all of a sudden think

00:01:35.092 --> 00:01:35.968
maybe I would do this?

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.572
- Yeah so I was in high school

00:01:37.572 --> 00:01:39.420
and I did TV production

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.714
and I did a lot of the producing,

00:01:40.714 --> 00:01:41.645
I was behind the scenes.

00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:42.509
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:43.896
- So when I played ice hockey,

00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:45.566
I used to have practice
super late at night,

00:01:45.566 --> 00:01:46.975
so I wouldn't get home till
like one or two in the morning.

00:01:46.975 --> 00:01:47.808
- Yeah.

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:50.102
- And I had this professor
who was a huge hockey fan

00:01:50.102 --> 00:01:52.753
so he knew about this career path

00:01:52.753 --> 00:01:54.664
that felt very farfetched in Florida.

00:01:54.664 --> 00:01:56.538
But he said, you know what,

00:01:56.538 --> 00:01:59.484
come in morning announcements
doesn't start for 30 minutes

00:01:59.484 --> 00:02:00.908
after the class,

00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:02.793
get a little quick cat nap and
then we'll go do the thing.

00:02:02.793 --> 00:02:04.532
So I was like, this is the best class.

00:02:04.532 --> 00:02:06.471
My GPA was terrible.

00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:09.038
And I started making the
commercial segments for the news

00:02:09.038 --> 00:02:11.683
and I did this terrible segment about kids

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:13.793
making sure they applied to college,

00:02:13.793 --> 00:02:16.217
which the irony of that was
I never applied to college.

00:02:16.217 --> 00:02:17.353
(laughing)

00:02:17.353 --> 00:02:19.778
So I'm sitting here doing
this commercial segment

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:20.611
and it was-

00:02:20.611 --> 00:02:21.444
- Selling people.

00:02:21.444 --> 00:02:23.534
- The peak of the Harry Potter stuff.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:24.887
And so I made this terrible commercial

00:02:24.887 --> 00:02:26.844
with like terrible VFX shocking people

00:02:26.844 --> 00:02:28.390
with wands about not going to college.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:29.223
- Sounds fun.

00:02:29.223 --> 00:02:30.282
- And my professor was like,

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.405
you should get into acting.

00:02:32.405 --> 00:02:33.955
- I love that he saw that.

00:02:33.955 --> 00:02:35.832
- Yeah with terrible VFX and a wand,

00:02:35.832 --> 00:02:37.530
he's like that dude's destined for-

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.863
And that was it.

00:02:39.828 --> 00:02:40.694
- That is awesome though.

00:02:40.694 --> 00:02:42.985
Like I feel like a teacher
is what pushed me to

00:02:42.985 --> 00:02:44.832
really have the confidence
to do what I do.

00:02:44.832 --> 00:02:45.665
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.498
- I feel like,

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:47.331
did you have a teacher like that that-

00:02:47.331 --> 00:02:48.164
- I love the classroom.

00:02:48.164 --> 00:02:49.837
Teachers made a big difference in my-

00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:50.920
I had some great teachers

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.297
and they lifted me way, way up.

00:02:54.297 --> 00:02:55.573
- Yeah, me too.

00:02:55.573 --> 00:02:56.924
They gave me such confidence.

00:02:56.924 --> 00:02:58.864
But Outer Banks is in season three,

00:02:58.864 --> 00:02:59.697
so congratulations for-

00:02:59.697 --> 00:03:00.530
- Thank you.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.726
(audience cheering &amp; clapping)

00:03:02.726 --> 00:03:03.609
- So is it true that you modeled

00:03:03.609 --> 00:03:05.205
your character after Kurt Cobain?

00:03:05.205 --> 00:03:06.227
- I did, yeah.

00:03:06.227 --> 00:03:09.431
- But you're pretty young
to even know Kurt Cobain.

00:03:09.431 --> 00:03:10.264
I love that.

00:03:10.264 --> 00:03:11.097
- Yeah.

00:03:11.097 --> 00:03:11.930
- My stepdad was a DJ.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:12.763
- Oh, okay.

00:03:12.763 --> 00:03:13.833
- Yeah so he was,

00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:15.761
he heavily influenced me by music.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.607
And I've always kind of,

00:03:17.607 --> 00:03:18.440
I don't know about you with characters,

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.352
but I always try to make a playlist

00:03:19.352 --> 00:03:20.479
with whatever I'm working with on.

00:03:20.479 --> 00:03:21.561
- So funny you should say that.

00:03:21.561 --> 00:03:23.204
Yes, I have,

00:03:23.204 --> 00:03:24.811
and I'm doing it even more now.

00:03:24.811 --> 00:03:26.695
Very deliberate playlist and-

00:03:26.695 --> 00:03:27.535
- For like mood and-

00:03:27.535 --> 00:03:28.368
- It does a lot for me.

00:03:28.368 --> 00:03:29.201
- Oh.

00:03:29.201 --> 00:03:30.205
- Yeah,

00:03:30.205 --> 00:03:31.038
so after the first season,

00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:32.296
he's sort of this happy-go-lucky kid

00:03:32.296 --> 00:03:35.253
and goes through a little bit of turmoil,

00:03:35.253 --> 00:03:37.495
but the second season is really about him

00:03:37.495 --> 00:03:39.246
internalizing a lot of that.

00:03:39.246 --> 00:03:40.201
So I met with Emmy,

00:03:40.201 --> 00:03:41.353
our costume director,

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:43.001
and she and I sort of sat down and said,

00:03:43.001 --> 00:03:44.543
okay this is the direction we're going,

00:03:44.543 --> 00:03:46.036
what are your thoughts?

00:03:46.036 --> 00:03:48.947
And I was listening to a
lot of Nirvana at the time,

00:03:48.947 --> 00:03:50.293
sort of building the character in my head.

00:03:50.293 --> 00:03:52.419
And I said, Kurt Cobain,
like let's do big flannels.

00:03:52.419 --> 00:03:54.661
Let's do things that
are out of the ordinary

00:03:54.661 --> 00:03:56.662
for where he normally is.

00:03:56.662 --> 00:04:00.609
And so, and sort of modeled
the imagery of the character-

00:04:00.609 --> 00:04:01.442
- [Kelly] The aesthetic of it, yeah.

00:04:01.442 --> 00:04:03.684
- With the dialogue in
the script going forward.

00:04:03.684 --> 00:04:05.864
So you're seeing the transition from,

00:04:05.864 --> 00:04:08.037
I'm excited about this
world of chasing treasure,

00:04:08.037 --> 00:04:09.955
to I miss my father and I don't know

00:04:09.955 --> 00:04:11.346
if I'm doing my friend's justice.

00:04:11.346 --> 00:04:13.540
So we kind of played
with the visual imagery

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.129
as much as we did to storyline itself so-

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.193
- That's cool.

00:04:16.193 --> 00:04:17.345
I like how much you think
about the character.

00:04:17.345 --> 00:04:18.978
Nobody, I never think about that

00:04:18.978 --> 00:04:19.811
when I'm watching something.

00:04:19.811 --> 00:04:20.973
I never think about all the backstory

00:04:20.973 --> 00:04:23.806
that goes into it or the
reasons like why you do so

00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:25.096
and the fact that you make playlists.

00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:26.165
That's cool.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:26.998
Yeah, it's fun.

00:04:26.998 --> 00:04:27.831
I think it's a fun time.

00:04:27.831 --> 00:04:28.664
- Yeah.

00:04:28.664 --> 00:04:29.977
I wanna hear your playlist
for your characters.

